c3=A.a([A.L(d5,"Payment in Cantonese Mahjong uses a fixed Faan-to-money table. It does NOT double each Faan - the common table is: 3F=$8, 4F=$16, 5F=$24, 6F=$32, 7F=$48, 8F=$64, 9F=$96, 10F=$128 (limit).",d6,d6),A.L(d5,"Common fixed table: 3F=$8, 4F=$16, 5F=$24, 6F=$32, 7F=$48, 8F=$64, 9F=$96, 10F=$128 (the cap). Payment rises steadily - NOT by doubling per Faan!",d6,d6),A.L(d5,"Who pays? (Half-fire / \u534a\u9283 system) If you win by discard: the DISCARDER pays the FULL amount. If you self-draw: each of the 3 opponents pays HALF the amount (so you collect 1.5x total).",d6,d6),A.L(d5,"Example: 3-Faan = $8. By discard: discarder pays the FULL $8. By self-draw: each of 3 opponents pays HALF ($4), so you collect $4 \xd7 3 = $12 total. Self-draw collects from all 3 but at half rate each.",d6,d6)],i4)
